  "body": "Fixes: #5974\n\n### Description\nConcurrent requests resolving the same hostname when the DNS cache was cold previously triggered separate, redundant lookups for each request.\n\nThis PR tracks in-flight lookups per hostname using an internal map in `DNSInstance`:\n- Concurrent requests for the same hostname join the in-flight resolution queue instead of initiating duplicate lookup calls.\n- Once resolution finishes, results are cached once in `storage`, and each waiting request independently selects an address using `pick()` (preserving round-robin distribution and family affinity).\n- If the lookup fails, in-flight state is cleared, all waiting callers receive the error, and subsequent requests can retry.\n\n### Tests\n- Added unit test in `test/interceptors/dns.js` verifying that concurrent requests share a single DNS lookup and subsequent requests use the cached result.\n- Added unit test verifying that lookup failures clear in-flight tracking and reject all waiting callers while allowing subsequent retries.",
